              model_answer:
                "Lister applied Pasteur's discovery that airborne microorganisms cause fermentation and putrefaction to open wounds. Lister realized that sepsis and gangrene in compound fractures were caused by airborne microbes entering open flesh, and proved that applying carbolic acid killed these germs, reducing post-operative mortality to zero in his eleven test cases.",
