              content:
                'Section 13: All existing and future sewers within the district of a local authority shall vest in and be under the control of such local authority, which shall cause them to be properly cleansed and emptied... Section 64: All existing public cisterns, pumps, wells, reservoirs, and conduits used for the gratuitous supply of water to inhabitants shall be maintained and kept plentifully supplied with pure and wholesome water by the local authority... Section 189: Every urban authority shall from time to time appoint a legally qualified medical practitioner as Medical Officer of Health, and shall appoint a fit and proper person to be Inspector of Nuisances... Section 116: The Medical Officer of Health may at all reasonable times inspect any animal, carcass, meat, poultry, fish, fruit, or vegetables exposed for sale, and if unfit for the food of man, seize the same.',
