              content:
                'Preventable pain is a blot upon any society which claims to be civilized... The collective principle asserts that the society protects itself against the hazards of nature and society by collective action. When a person is sick, we do not ask whether he can afford the treatment; we ask what treatment he needs... Existing hospital facilities in this country are a chaotic patchwork of bankrupt voluntary institutions and obsolete poor-law infirmaries. In many rural counties and small industrial towns, there is not a single hospital capable of performing modern thoracic or neurological surgery. We must nationalize the hospitals, plan medical facilities rationally across regional hospital boards, and ensure that the best specialist care is available equally in the mining valleys of South Wales as in Harley Street.',
