                'The state of the ground defies description. The communication trenches have ceased to exist, having been obliterated by continuous heavy shelling and turned into channels of liquid clay three to four feet deep. Relieving stretcher squads took six hours to convey a single severely wounded casualty over a distance of barely two miles from the frontline aid post to the dressing station. Four bearers carried the stretcher while two accompanied them with poles to haul the bearers out when they sank to their waists. Several walking wounded fell into water-filled shell craters in the dark and were drowned before assistance could reach them.',
