              citation:
                'The National Archives, Kew (WO 95/Infantry Battalion Standing Orders / Crown Copyright).',
              content:
                "1. Every man before entering the frontline trenches must grease his feet thoroughly with whale oil provided at company stores.\n2. Company commanders will ensure that every soldier carries two pairs of dry socks in his haversack. A dry pair must be put on every twelve hours, and the wet pair dried around the neck inside the tunic.\n3. Platoon officers will hold a daily foot inspection in the firebays. Every soldier will remove his boots and puttees in the presence of an officer or NCO, rub his feet with oil, and rub his comrade's feet. Any officer whose platoon reports preventable cases of trench foot will be required to explain why disciplinary standing orders were neglected.",
