              content:
                'Trench Fever (Pyrexia of Unknown Origin) has been responsible for the loss of more rifle strength than any other single disease on the Western Front. Over 15% of all non-combat hospital admissions are due to this relapsing 5-day fever, which causes severe headaches, high pyrexia, and agonizing pain in the shins and back.\nOur laboratory investigations confirm beyond doubt that the disease is transmitted by the body louse (Pediculus humanus). The infection is not inoculated by the bite of the insect itself, but by the soldier scratching louse excreta into broken skin. Complete eradication depends entirely on regular steam delousing of uniforms in Divisional de-lousing plants and the frequent provision of clean clothing.',
