          caption:
            'The Thomas Splint in Practice: Designed by Welsh orthopaedic surgeon Hugh Owen Thomas and introduced to the Western Front in 1915 by his nephew Robert Jones. Continuous tension on the leg kept broken femur bone ends aligned, preventing severed femoral arteries and reducing fracture mortality from 80% to 20%.',
